{"id":"G2288","lemma":"θάνατος","transliteration":"thanatos","sayIt":"thanatos","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun, masculine","gloss":"death","meaning":"θάνατος, -ου, ὁ (θνήσκω),\n[in LXX chiefly for מָוֶת ,מוּת, sometimes דֶּבֶר ;]\ndeath;\n1. of the death of the body, whether natural or violent: Jhn.11:13, Php.2:27, Heb.7:23, al; opposite to ζωή, Rom.8:38, Php.1:20; of the death of Christ, Rom.5:10, Php.3:10, Heb.2:9; ῥυέσθαι (σώζειν) ἐκ θ., 2Co.1:10, Heb.5:7; περίλυπος ἕως θανάτου, Mat.26:38, Mrk.14:34; μέχρι (ἄχρι), Php.2:8, Rev.2:10; πληγὴ θανάτου, a deadly wound. Rev.13:3; ἰδεῖν θάνατον, Luk.2:26, Heb.11:5; γεύεσθαι θανάτου, Mrk.9:1; ἔνοχος θανάτου, Mrk.14:64; θανάτῳ τελευτᾶν ( Exo.21:17, מוּת יוּמָת), Mrk.7:10; death personified, Rom.6:9, 1Co.15:26, Rev.21:4; pl., of deadly perils, 2Co.11:23.\n2. Of spiritual death: Jhn.5:24 8:51, Rom.7:10, Jas.1:15, 5:20, 1Jn.3:14 5:16, al.; of eternal death, Rom.1:32 7:5, al.; ὁ θ. ὁ δεύτερος, Rev.2:11 21:8 (cf. Cremer, 283ff.; DB, iii, 114ff.; DCG, i, 791f.).\n(AS)","glosses":["death","must be put to death","death sentence","die","kind of death","death is"],"count":106,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-4","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"of death","kjv":"of death"}},{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":21,"renderings":{"bsb":"death","kjv":"death"}},{"chapterId":"mat-15","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"must be put to death"}},{"chapterId":"mat-16","v":28,"renderings":{"bsb":"death","kjv":"of death"}},{"chapterId":"mat-20","v":18,"renderings":{"bsb":"death"}},{"chapterId":"mat-26","v":38,"renderings":{"bsb":"of death","kjv":"death"}},{"chapterId":"mat-26","v":66,"renderings":{"bsb":"to die"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-7","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"must be put to death"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-9","v":1,"renderings":{"bsb":"death","kjv":"of death"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-10","v":33,"renderings":{"bsb":"to death","kjv":"to death"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-13","v":12,"renderings":{"bsb":"death","kjv":"death"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-14","v":34,"renderings":{"bsb":"death